# AI Waiting UX — How This Fits Together

This module was generated by the `ai-waiting-ux` skill. It implements the four properties from the Doherty Threshold brief:

1. Continuous progress (every SDK event surfaced)
2. Live ETA (recomputed on every event)
3. OS notifications (Web Notifications + idle heartbeats)
4. Persistent readable log (LogSink: JSONL on Node, IndexedDB on browser)

## Mental model

> Treat a Claude Agent SDK session as an event-sourced long-running operation. Stream every SDK event into a normalized log. Derive UI, ETA, notifications, and audit trail from that single stream. Surface progress continuously so the user never has to invent a ritual to find out whether the agent is still alive.

## Layers

```
SDK → SdkAdapter → AgentEvent[] → agentReducer → SessionState
                                              → LogSink (durable)
                                              → ClientTransport (browser)
                                              → useNotifications (OS)
```

